'''The 2016 United States House of Representatives elections''' will be held on November 8, 2016. Elections will be held to elect representatives from all 435 [[List of United States congressional districts|congressional districts]] across each of the 50 [[U.S. state]]s. [[Delegate (United States Congress)|Non-voting delegates]] from the [[District of Columbia]] and the five inhabited [[Insular area|U.S. territories]]<ref group="Note">Including the [[Resident Commissioner of Puerto Rico]], who serves a four-year term.</ref> will also be elected. The winners of this election will serve in the [[115th United States Congress]], with seats apportioned among the states based on the [[2010 United States Census]]. In October 2015, [[Speaker of the House]] [[John Boehner]] resigned his position; the House [[Speaker of the United States House of Representatives election, October 2015|elected]] Congressman [[Paul Ryan]] of [[Wisconsin]] as his replacement. [[Nancy Pelosi]] continues to lead House Democrats as [[Minority Leader]].

The [[United States presidential election, 2016|2016 Presidential election]], [[United States Senate elections, 2016|2016 Senate elections]], [[United States gubernatorial elections, 2016|2016 gubernatorial elections]], and many [[United States elections, 2016|state and local elections]] will also be held on this date.

